@startuml
title DineFlow - General Use Cases
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide empty members
skinparam usecaseBackgroundColor #EAF4FF
skinparam usecaseBorderColor #3D5368

left to right direction
actor Customer
actor Waiter
actor Manager
actor "Payment Provider" as Provider
actor "Restaurant/POS" as POS
rectangle "DineFlow" {
 usecase "Discover restaurants\nFR-001-FR-004, FR-006" as Discover
 usecase "Reserve a table\nFR-005" as Book
 usecase "Create a pre-order\nFR-007" as Order
 usecase "Prepay / pay bill\nFR-008, FR-011" as Pay
 usecase "Call / receive waiter request\nFR-010, FR-014" as Call
 usecase "Manage reservations / pre-orders\nFR-012-FR-013" as Manage
 usecase "Exchange restaurant information\nFR-009, AC-001, AC-005" as Sync
 usecase "Later visit capabilities\nFR-015-FR-026; Should/Could" as Later #FFF4D6
}
Customer -- Discover
Customer -- Book
Customer -- Order
Customer -- Pay
Customer -- Call
Customer -- Later
Waiter -- Call
Manager -- Manage
Provider -- Pay
POS -- Sync
legend bottom
Blue: recorded capabilities; amber: later Should/Could scope.
Waiter and Manager are roles; one employee may play both per restaurant.
P-STAFF role allocation and P-PAY provider delegation remain proposed.
Design stage; requirement IDs and priority labels remain authoritative.
endlegend
@enduml
